Consider a birational diagram $$\label{eq:step-diagram}
 X^-\xrightarrow{\,f^-\,} Z
 \xleftarrow{\,f^+\,}X^+,$$ where the varieties are normal fourfolds, the morphisms have connected fibres, $f^+$ is small, and the divisors $D^\pm=K_{X^\pm}+B^\pm$ are $\mathbb Q$-Cartier. The boundary on $X^+$ is the strict transform of $f^-_*B^-$, and $-D^-$ and $D^+$ are ample over $Z$.

Set $$\label{eq:branch-loci}
 C=p(Q)_{\mathrm{red}},\qquad
 P=(p^{-1}C)_{\mathrm{red}}.$$

